    "description": "Help › Auto-scroll › Two modes — point 3"
  },
  "helpAutoScrollS2Heading": "What \"bars\" means",
  "@helpAutoScrollS2Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Auto-scroll › section heading"
  },
  "helpAutoScrollS2P1": "A bar (also called a measure) is a musical unit of time.",
  "@helpAutoScrollS2P1": {
    "description": "Help › Auto-scroll › What \"bars\" means — point 1"
  },
  "helpAutoScrollS2P2": "A song that names no tala uses common 4/4 time, so one bar is 4 beats.",
  "@helpAutoScrollS2P2": {
    "description": "Help › Auto-scroll › What \"bars\" means — point 2"
  },
  "helpAutoScrollS2P3": "A song with a '{tala}' line counts that tala''s own beats instead, so a misra chapu song has 7 beats to the bar.",
  "@helpAutoScrollS2P3": {
    "description": "Help › Auto-scroll › What \"bars\" means — point 3"
  },
  "helpAutoScrollS2P4": "Songs open at 32 bars. Change the count by double-tapping the sheet — each double-tap adds or removes 4 bars.",
  "@helpAutoScrollS2P4": {
    "description": "Help › Auto-scroll › What \"bars\" means — point 4"
