  },
  "helpFullScreenS3P2": "The padlock locks the screen — see below.",
  "@helpFullScreenS3P2": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › The buttons in the bar — point 2"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS3P3": "The bell turns Stage Quiet Mode on and off — see below.",
  "@helpFullScreenS3P3": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › The buttons in the bar — point 3"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS3P4": "M and T pick Manual or Tempo, and the round button plays or pauses.",
  "@helpFullScreenS3P4": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › The buttons in the bar — point 4"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS3P5": "The bars icon opens the pitch pipe and shruti box.",
  "@helpFullScreenS3P5": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › The buttons in the bar — point 5"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS3P6": "The - and + at the end change the speed in Manual mode and the bar count in Tempo mode, the same as the double-taps.",
  "@helpFullScreenS3P6": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › The buttons in the bar — point 6"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS3P7": "The line under the buttons repeats the key, the BPM and, in Tempo mode, the length.",
  "@helpFullScreenS3P7": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › The buttons in the bar — point 7"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS4Heading": "Lock the screen",
  "@helpFullScreenS4Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › section heading"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS4P1": "Tap the padlock to lock Stage View. The tap controls are then switched off, so a sleeve or a stray hand cannot change your speed or pause you mid-song.",
  "@helpFullScreenS4P1": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Lock the screen — point 1"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS4P2": "The control bar hides and a small \"Stage Locked\" chip appears in the top right.",
  "@helpFullScreenS4P2": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Lock the screen — point 2"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS4P3": "Tap that chip, or press Back, to unlock. It asks for your fingerprint, or the PIN, pattern or password the phone already uses.",
  "@helpFullScreenS4P3": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Lock the screen — point 3"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS4P4": "On a phone with no screen lock set up there is nothing to check against, so it simply unlocks.",
  "@helpFullScreenS4P4": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Lock the screen — point 4"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS4P5": "If the check cannot run at all, the stage unlocks anyway and says so. The lock is there to stop stray touches, so it will never shut you out.",
  "@helpFullScreenS4P5": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Lock the screen — point 5"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS5Heading": "Stage Quiet Mode",
  "@helpFullScreenS5Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › section heading"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS5P1": "Tap the bell to mute the ringer and notification alerts while you play, so a call cannot chime through the PA.",
  "@helpFullScreenS5P1": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Stage Quiet Mode — point 1"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS5P2": "The app''s own sound is left alone — the metronome click, the pitch cue and the drone all keep working.",
  "@helpFullScreenS5P2": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Stage Quiet Mode — point 2"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS5P3": "The icon turns red only once the phone has really gone silent. Tap it again, leave full screen, or leave the song, and your normal ringer setting comes back — even if the app was closed.",
  "@helpFullScreenS5P3": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Stage Quiet Mode — point 3"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS5P4": "The first time, Android may ask you to allow \"Do Not Disturb access\" for LyricChord. Tap Open settings in the message, turn it on, then tap the bell again.",
  "@helpFullScreenS5P4": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Stage Quiet Mode — point 4"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS5P5": "iPhones do not let apps change the ringer, so the bell is not shown there. Use the ring/silent switch instead.",
  "@helpFullScreenS5P5": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Stage Quiet Mode — point 5"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS6Heading": "Getting back",
  "@helpFullScreenS6Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › section heading"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS6P1": "Press Back, or tap once and use the exit button in the control bar.",
  "@helpFullScreenS6P1": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Getting back — point 1"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS6P2": "That leaves full screen only — you are still on the same song. Press Back again to return to your songbook.",
  "@helpFullScreenS6P2": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Getting back — point 2"
  },
  "helpFullScreenS6P3": "Swiping sideways does not change the song while you are full screen, so a stray touch cannot throw the wrong song up mid-song.",
  "@helpFullScreenS6P3": {
    "description": "Help › Full screen › Getting back — point 3"
  },
  "titleHelpMetronome": "Metronome",
  "@titleHelpMetronome": {
    "description": "Help › topic title (metronome)"
  },
  "helpMetronomeSummary": "Keep the beat at the song tempo",
  "@helpMetronomeSummary": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › one-line summary on the hub card"
  },
  "helpMetronomeIntro": "The metronome keeps time while you perform. Its speed comes from each song''s BPM (beats per minute), which you set in the song editor.",
  "@helpMetronomeIntro": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › opening paragraph"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS1Heading": "Turn it on",
  "@helpMetronomeS1Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › section heading"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS1P1": "Go to Settings > General > Metronome.",
  "@helpMetronomeS1P1": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Turn it on — point 1"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS1P2": "Switch on \"Enable metronome\".",
  "@helpMetronomeS1P2": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Turn it on — point 2"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS1P3": "The setting is saved and stays on after you restart the app.",
  "@helpMetronomeS1P3": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Turn it on — point 3"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS2Heading": "Flash and Click",
  "@helpMetronomeS2Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › section heading"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS2P1": "Flash blinks on every beat — handy when the sound is muted.",
  "@helpMetronomeS2P1": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Flash and Click — point 1"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS2P2": "Click plays a short tick on every beat.",
  "@helpMetronomeS2P2": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Flash and Click — point 2"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS2P3": "You can use either, both, or neither.",
  "@helpMetronomeS2P3": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Flash and Click — point 3"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS2P4": "Flash and Click stay greyed out until the metronome is enabled.",
  "@helpMetronomeS2P4": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Flash and Click — point 4"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS2P5": "Click volume sets how loud the tick is. The tick uses the media volume, so raise the volume buttons while a song is open if you cannot hear it.",
  "@helpMetronomeS2P5": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Flash and Click — point 5"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS2P6": "Tap \"Test the sound\" in Metronome settings to hear one bar without opening a song.",
  "@helpMetronomeS2P6": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Flash and Click — point 6"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS3Heading": "Beats in a bar",
  "@helpMetronomeS3Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › section heading"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS3P1": "Pick 2, 3, 4 or 6 beats in a bar in Metronome settings.",
  "@helpMetronomeS3P1": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Beats in a bar — point 1"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS3P2": "With \"Accent beat 1\" on, the first beat of every bar is louder and higher, so you can hear where the bar starts.",
  "@helpMetronomeS3P2": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Beats in a bar — point 2"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS3P3": "While the beat runs, the button counts the beat number — 1, 2, 3, 4 — so you can see your place even with the sound off.",
  "@helpMetronomeS3P3": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Beats in a bar — point 3"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS4Heading": "Set the tempo",
  "@helpMetronomeS4Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › section heading"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS4P1": "By default the beat speed follows the song''s BPM.",
  "@helpMetronomeS4P1": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Set the tempo — point 1"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS4P2": "Change a song''s BPM by editing the song.",
  "@helpMetronomeS4P2": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Set the tempo — point 2"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS4P3": "Long press the metronome button to set the speed by hand: use - and +, drag the slider, or tap \"Tap tempo\" along with the music.",
  "@helpMetronomeS4P3": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Set the tempo — point 3"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS4P4": "A tempo you set by hand lasts for this session only. Tap \"Use song tempo\" to go back to the song''s own speed.",
  "@helpMetronomeS4P4": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Set the tempo — point 4"
  },
  "helpMetronomeS4P5": "A song with no saved BPM still works — the metronome uses the last speed you used.",
  "@helpMetronomeS4P5": {
    "description": "Help › Metronome › Set the tempo — point 5"
  },
  "titleHelpPitchPipeDrone": "Pitch Pipe & Drone",
  "@titleHelpPitchPipeDrone": {
    "description": "Help › topic title (pitch-pipe-drone)"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneSummary": "Reference pitch cues and a steady shruti box drone",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneSummary": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › one-line summary on the hub card"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneIntro": "A fully offline sound generator: a short reference note to start on, and a steady shruti box drone to sing against. Nothing is downloaded and no sound files ship with the app — the tones are built as you press the button.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneIntro": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › opening paragraph"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS1Heading": "What the drone does — and does not do",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS1Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › section heading"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS1P1": "The drone holds ONE steady pair of notes for as long as it is on.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS1P1": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › What the drone does — and does not do — point 1"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS1P2": "It does NOT follow the tune, the words, or the chords. It never changes until you change it.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS1P2": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › What the drone does — and does not do — point 2"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS1P3": "Think of it as a tuning fork that never stops, so your ear stays anchored while you sing.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS1P3": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › What the drone does — and does not do — point 3"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS2Heading": "Where to find it",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS2Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › section heading"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS2P1": "Open a song and tap the pitch button (the bars icon) next to the metronome.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS2P1": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Where to find it — point 1"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS2P2": "It is in the Stage Mode bar too, next to the play button.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS2P2": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Where to find it — point 2"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS2P3": "Settings → General → Pitch Pipe & Drone sets the defaults and has Test buttons.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS2P3": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Where to find it — point 3"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS3Heading": "Pitch Cue (called Chord Cue in Western)",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS3Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › section heading"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS3P1": "Tap \"Pitch Cue\" to hear a 2-second reference note. It is a digital pitch pipe: it sounds your Sa (or the key you picked), then stops on its own.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS3P1": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Pitch Cue (called Chord Cue in Western) — point 1"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS3P2": "Use it to find your starting note before you begin singing.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS3P2": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Pitch Cue (called Chord Cue in Western) — point 2"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS3P3": "In Western mode the same button is named \"Chord Cue\" and plays the whole chord — bass, root, third and fifth — because Western players want the chord, not one note. Major or minor follows the quality you picked.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS3P3": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Pitch Cue (called Chord Cue in Western) — point 3"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS3P4": "The length is fixed at 2 seconds and there is no setting for it. That is long enough to hear the pitch clearly and short enough not to get in the way. The button says \"(2s)\" so you know what you will get before you tap it.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS3P4": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Pitch Cue (called Chord Cue in Western) — point 4"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS3P5": "If you want a tone that lasts longer, use the Shruti Drone instead. That is what it is for.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS3P5": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Pitch Cue (called Chord Cue in Western) — point 5"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS4Heading": "Cue or drone — which one?",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS4Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › section heading"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS4P1": "Cue: one short sound that stops by itself. For finding the note before you start.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS4P1": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Cue or drone — which one? — point 1"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS4P2": "Drone: keeps sounding until you stop it. For singing against while you practise or perform.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS4P2": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Cue or drone — which one? — point 2"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS4P3": "Both are built inside the app the moment you press the button. Nothing is downloaded and no sound files ship with the app.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS4P3": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Cue or drone — which one? — point 3"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS5Heading": "Shruti box drone",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS5Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › section heading"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS5P1": "Tap \"Shruti Drone\" to start a continuous background hum.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS5P1": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Shruti box drone — point 1"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS5P2": "Choose Sa + Pa (the fifth) for most music, or Sa + Ma (the fourth) for ragas that leave out Pa, such as Malkauns or Marwa.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS5P2": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Shruti box drone — point 2"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS5P3": "The two notes are tuned in pure ratios (3:2 and 4:3), the way a real drone instrument sounds — not in equal temperament.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS5P3": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Shruti box drone — point 3"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS5P4": "The drone keeps playing until you stop it, so you can practise without it cutting out.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS5P4": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Shruti box drone — point 4"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS6Heading": "Indian and Western naming",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS6Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › section heading"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS6P1": "Sa is movable, so the app must know which actual pitch your Sa is. Set it in Settings → \"Your Sa (Shruti)\".",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS6P1": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Indian and Western naming — point 1"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS6P2": "A song with a raga is named the Indian way: \"5 kattai\" for Carnatic, \"safed 5\" for Hindustani. The tala decides which. No Western letters appear on an Indian sheet.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS6P2": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Indian and Western naming — point 2"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS6P3": "A song without a raga is named the Western way: just \"G\".",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS6P3": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Indian and Western naming — point 3"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS6P4": "A Western song opens on the song''s own key. An Indian song opens on your Sa, because the notation is written relative to Sa.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS6P4": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Indian and Western naming — point 4"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS7Heading": "Text size for the stage",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS7Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › section heading"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS7P1": "The same sheet is read on a phone in your hand and on a stand two steps away, so the pitch sheet carries a text size setting.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS7P1": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Text size for the stage — point 1"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS7P2": "Pick one of five sizes — 85%, 95%, 100%, 115% or 130% — from the chips at the bottom of the pitch sheet.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS7P2": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Text size for the stage — point 2"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS7P3": "Settings → General → Pitch Pipe & Drone has the same chips, so you can set it before a gig.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS7P3": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Text size for the stage — point 3"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS7P4": "It multiplies the sheet text size everywhere, not only in full screen.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS7P4": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Text size for the stage — point 4"
  },
  "helpPitchPipeDroneS7P5": "Pinching the sheet with two fingers still works and is the quicker way to nudge one song.",
  "@helpPitchPipeDroneS7P5": {
    "description": "Help › Pitch Pipe & Drone › Text size for the stage — point 5"
  },
  "titleHelpMelody": "Melody Lines",
  "@titleHelpMelody": {
    "description": "Help › topic title (melody)"
  },
  "helpMelodySummary": "Write the tune under the words, then hear it.",
  "@helpMelodySummary": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › one-line summary on the hub card"
  },
  "helpMelodyIntro": "A chord sheet tells you the words and tells the accompanist what to play. It does not tell you the tune. A melody line adds that. Write '{melody}' under a lyric line and the app draws the beats and hums them back, so you can learn a song you have never heard.",
  "@helpMelodyIntro": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › opening paragraph"
  },
  "helpMelodyS1Heading": "Writing one",
  "@helpMelodyS1Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › section heading"
  },
  "helpMelodyS1P1": "Put a line starting with '{melody}' under the lyric line it belongs to.",
  "@helpMelodyS1P1": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Writing one — point 1"
  },
  "helpMelodyS1P2": "Example: '{melody}' P ,  M2 | M2!G3~ ,  | R2 S",
  "@helpMelodyS1P2": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Writing one — point 2"
  },
  "helpMelodyS1P3": "Beats are separated by spaces. One beat, one space.",
  "@helpMelodyS1P3": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Writing one — point 3"
  },
  "helpMelodyS1P4": "The words and chords above it do not change at all.",
  "@helpMelodyS1P4": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Writing one — point 4"
  },
  "helpMelodyS1P5": "You do not have to type it. In the editor, More options → \"Melody keypad\" gives you a pad of all sixteen swaras and every mark, draws the beats as you tap, and counts \"6 of 8 beats\" until the line fills the tala.",
  "@helpMelodyS1P5": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Writing one — point 5"
  },
  "helpMelodyS1P6": "With the cursor already on a '{melody}' line, the keypad loads that line so you can fix it instead of deleting it first.",
  "@helpMelodyS1P6": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Writing one — point 6"
  },
  "helpMelodyS1P7": "A block of published Carnatic notation can be turned into melody lines in one go — see the Indian songs topic.",
  "@helpMelodyS1P7": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Writing one — point 7"
  },
  "helpMelodyS2Heading": "The five marks",
  "@helpMelodyS2Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › section heading"
  },
  "helpMelodyS2P1": "A comma ( , ) holds the note before it for one more beat.",
  "@helpMelodyS2P1": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › The five marks — point 1"
  },
  "helpMelodyS2P2": "A bar ( | ) shows where a new tala group starts. It takes no time.",
  "@helpMelodyS2P2": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › The five marks — point 2"
  },
  "helpMelodyS2P3": "A hyphen ( - ) joins notes that share one beat: G3-R2 is half a beat each.",
  "@helpMelodyS2P3": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › The five marks — point 3"
  },
  "helpMelodyS2P4": "A bang ( ! ) slides into a note. M2!G3 starts the slide at Ma. A bare !G3 is a short slide in from just under Ga.",
  "@helpMelodyS2P4": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › The five marks — point 4"
  },
  "helpMelodyS2P5": "A tilde ( ~ ) shakes the note.",
  "@helpMelodyS2P5": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › The five marks — point 5"
  },
  "helpMelodyS3Heading": "Naming the notes",
  "@helpMelodyS3Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › section heading"
  },
  "helpMelodyS3P1": "A bare name is the note from the plain Sa Re Ga Ma Pa Dha Ni row, so Ma on its own is Ma1.",
  "@helpMelodyS3P1": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Naming the notes — point 1"
  },
  "helpMelodyS3P2": "A digit names the exact one: Ma2 is the raised Ma, R1 R2 R3 are the three Ris.",
  "@helpMelodyS3P2": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Naming the notes — point 2"
  },
  "helpMelodyS3P3": "Ma2 and M2 mean the same note. Use full names in chords and short letters in melody lines, or whichever reads better.",
  "@helpMelodyS3P3": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Naming the notes — point 3"
  },
  "helpMelodyS3P4": "The raga never changes what a name means, so nothing is guessed.",
  "@helpMelodyS3P4": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Naming the notes — point 4"
  },
  "helpMelodyS3P5": "A dot in front drops a note an octave (.N3). An apostrophe after raises it (S'').",
  "@helpMelodyS3P5": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Naming the notes — point 5"
  },
  "helpMelodyS4Heading": "Hearing it",
  "@helpMelodyS4Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › section heading"
  },
  "helpMelodyS4P1": "Add '{tonic: 1 kattai}' so the app knows where your Sa really is. Without it the beats still draw, but nothing can play.",
  "@helpMelodyS4P1": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Hearing it — point 1"
  },
  "helpMelodyS4P2": "Add '{tala: misra chapu}' so the beats are grouped correctly.",
  "@helpMelodyS4P2": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Hearing it — point 2"
  },
  "helpMelodyS4P3": "The song tempo sets the speed.",
  "@helpMelodyS4P3": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Hearing it — point 3"
  },
  "helpMelodyS4P4": "Tap the play button beside a melody line to hum it.",
  "@helpMelodyS4P4": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Hearing it — point 4"
  },
  "helpMelodyS4P5": "To read the words without the tune rows, open the overflow menu → Performance controls and turn Show melody off. Full screen never draws the melody rows.",
  "@helpMelodyS4P5": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Hearing it — point 5"
  },
  "helpMelodyS4P6": "Turn on Loop to repeat the line, or Half speed to learn it slowly.",
  "@helpMelodyS4P6": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Hearing it — point 6"
  },
  "helpMelodyS4P7": "Start the shruti drone first — a tune is much easier to hear against a drone than on its own.",
  "@helpMelodyS4P7": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › Hearing it — point 7"
  },
  "helpMelodyS5Heading": "What it can and cannot do",
  "@helpMelodyS5Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › section heading"
  },
  "helpMelodyS5P1": "It shows you where the notes go and how long each one lasts.",
  "@helpMelodyS5P1": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › What it can and cannot do — point 1"
  },
  "helpMelodyS5P2": "It does not shape them the way a singer does. Listen to a recording for that.",
  "@helpMelodyS5P2": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › What it can and cannot do — point 2"
  },
  "helpMelodyS5P3": "Every song needs a person who knows the tune to type it in. There is no shortcut.",
  "@helpMelodyS5P3": {
    "description": "Help › Melody Lines › What it can and cannot do — point 3"
  },
  "titleHelpIndianSongs": "Indian songs",
  "@titleHelpIndianSongs": {
    "description": "Help › topic title (indian-songs)"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsSummary": "Swaras, raga, tala, and where your Sa is",
  "@helpIndianSongsSummary": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › one-line summary on the hub card"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsIntro": "An Indian song is written in swaras — Sa Re Ga Ma Pa Dha Ni — not in chords, and those names are relative to Sa rather than to a fixed pitch. The app treats such a song differently all the way through.",
  "@helpIndianSongsIntro": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › opening paragraph"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS1Heading": "Mark the song as Indian",
  "@helpIndianSongsS1Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › section heading"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS1P1": "In the editor, set \"Notation\" to Carnatic or Hindustani.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS1P1": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Mark the song as Indian — point 1"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS1P2": "The \"Original key\" box is replaced by Raga and Tala, because an Indian sheet has no key to transpose.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS1P2": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Mark the song as Indian — point 2"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS1P3": "Switching back to Western clears the raga and tala, so an old value can never make the song look Indian again.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS1P3": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Mark the song as Indian — point 3"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS2Heading": "The note under the Tala box",
  "@helpIndianSongsS2Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › section heading"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS2P1": "Typing a tala that belongs to the other tradition — Keherwa on a Carnatic song, say — shows a short note under the box.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS2P1": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › The note under the Tala box — point 1"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS2P2": "It is advice only. It never stops you saving. The app knows a fixed list of tala names and yours may simply not be on it.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS2P2": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › The note under the Tala box — point 2"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS2P3": "The tala also decides how many beats are in a bar for Tempo auto-scroll and for the beat grid under a melody line.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS2P3": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › The note under the Tala box — point 3"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS3Heading": "What changes on the song screen",
  "@helpIndianSongsS3Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › section heading"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS3P1": "No Western letter is shown. The status line reads \"Auto-scroll · 120 BPM\", with the raga and tala on the line below it.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS3P1": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › What changes on the song screen — point 1"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS3P2": "There is no transpose control, because a swara does not move.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS3P2": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › What changes on the song screen — point 2"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS3P3": "The menu offers \"Swara Reference\" in place of Chord Reference.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS3P3": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › What changes on the song screen — point 3"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS3P4": "The pitch sheet opens on your saved Sa instead of a song key, and names it the Indian way — \"5 kattai\" for Carnatic, \"safed 5\" for Hindustani.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS3P4": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › What changes on the song screen — point 4"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS4Heading": "Lines you can put in the words",
  "@helpIndianSongsS4Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › section heading"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS4P1": "'{tonic: 1 kattai}' says where your Sa really is. A melody line cannot be played without it.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS4P1": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Lines you can put in the words — point 1"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS4P2": "'{tala: misra chapu}' groups the beats.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS4P2": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Lines you can put in the words — point 2"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS4P3": "'{sruti: madhyama}' marks a song sung with the drone''s Pa string dropped to shuddha madhyamam, as Yamunakalyani usually is. The written Sa then sounds a fourth higher.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS4P3": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Lines you can put in the words — point 3"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS4P4": "'{melody}' lines hold the tune — see the Melody Lines topic.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS4P4": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Lines you can put in the words — point 4"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS4P5": "All of these live in the song text, so import and export carry them through unchanged.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS4P5": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Lines you can put in the words — point 5"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS5Heading": "Paste published notation",
  "@helpIndianSongsS5Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › section heading"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS5P1": "In the editor, More options → \"Paste Carnatic\" takes a block copied from a book or a page and turns it into '{melody}' lines.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS5P1": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Paste published notation — point 1"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS5P2": "Published notation has no single standard: on some pages a capital letter means a longer note, on others it means a higher octave.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS5P2": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Paste published notation — point 2"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS5P3": "So the app reads the block both ways, checks each against the song''s tala, and tells you which one fitted and by how much — like \"1 of 1 cycles fit, read with case means note length\".",
  "@helpIndianSongsS5P3": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Paste published notation — point 3"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS5P4": "Where the two ways tie it says so instead of guessing.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS5P4": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Paste published notation — point 4"
  },
  "helpIndianSongsS5P5": "It will not choose between the two Ma-s on its own. That is raga grammar, not arithmetic — but it points out the phrase that decides it.",
  "@helpIndianSongsS5P5": {
    "description": "Help › Indian songs › Paste published notation — point 5"
  },
  "titleHelpSelectSongs": "Select Songs",
  "@titleHelpSelectSongs": {
    "description": "Help › topic title (select-songs)"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsSummary": "Act on several songs at once",
  "@helpSelectSongsSummary": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › one-line summary on the hub card"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsIntro": "Selection mode lets you choose many songs together and then export or delete them in one step.",
  "@helpSelectSongsIntro": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › opening paragraph"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS1Heading": "Start selecting",
  "@helpSelectSongsS1Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › section heading"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS1P1": "On the Songs list, long-press any song to start selection mode.",
  "@helpSelectSongsS1P1": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › Start selecting — point 1"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS1P2": "Tap more songs to add them to the selection.",
  "@helpSelectSongsS1P2": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › Start selecting — point 2"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS1P3": "The top bar shows how many songs are selected.",
  "@helpSelectSongsS1P3": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › Start selecting — point 3"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS2Heading": "Select all",
  "@helpSelectSongsS2Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › section heading"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS2P1": "Use the \"Select all\" icon in the top bar to pick every visible song.",
  "@helpSelectSongsS2P1": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › Select all — point 1"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS2P2": "Tap it again (\"Deselect all\") to clear the selection.",
  "@helpSelectSongsS2P2": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › Select all — point 2"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS3Heading": "What you can do",
  "@helpSelectSongsS3Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › section heading"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS3P1": "Export the selected songs as one ChordPro file.",
  "@helpSelectSongsS3P1": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › What you can do — point 1"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS3P2": "Delete the selected songs from your library.",
  "@helpSelectSongsS3P2": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › What you can do — point 2"
  },
  "helpSelectSongsS3P3": "Tap the X on the top-left to leave selection mode without changes.",
  "@helpSelectSongsS3P3": {
    "description": "Help › Select Songs › What you can do — point 3"
  },
  "titleHelpImport": "Import",
  "@titleHelpImport": {
    "description": "Help › topic title (import)"
  },
  "helpImportSummary": "Bring songs into the app",
  "@helpImportSummary": {
    "description": "Help › Import › one-line summary on the hub card"
  },
  "helpImportIntro": "Import adds songs from ChordPro or plain text files into your library. Reading is defensive — broken or unreadable files are skipped safely and never break the app.",
  "@helpImportIntro": {
    "description": "Help › Import › opening paragraph"
  },
  "helpImportS1Heading": "Supported file types",
  "@helpImportS1Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Import › section heading"
  },
  "helpImportS1P1": "You can pick files ending in .cho, .pro, .chordpro, or .txt.",
  "@helpImportS1P1": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Supported file types — point 1"
  },
  "helpImportS1P2": "ChordPro files are plain text files that use simple tags for chords and headers.",
  "@helpImportS1P2": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Supported file types — point 2"
  },
  "helpImportS1P3": "You can pick one file or multiple files at the same time.",
  "@helpImportS1P3": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Supported file types — point 3"
  },
  "helpImportS2Heading": "Multiple songs in one file",
  "@helpImportS2Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Import › section heading"
  },
  "helpImportS2P1": "A single file can contain many songs.",
  "@helpImportS2P1": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Multiple songs in one file — point 1"
  },
  "helpImportS2P2": "Put '{new_song}' or '{ns}' on its own line between songs to separate them. This is the same separator used when you export your whole songbook.",
  "@helpImportS2P2": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Multiple songs in one file — point 2"
  },
  "helpImportS2P3": "You can also separate songs by starting a new '{title: ...}' or '{t: ...}' tag. The app automatically detects where the new song begins.",
  "@helpImportS2P3": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Multiple songs in one file — point 3"
  },
  "helpImportS3Heading": "Text files without tags",
  "@helpImportS3Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Import › section heading"
  },
  "helpImportS3P1": "A plain text file with no tags is imported safely as one song.",
  "@helpImportS3P1": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Text files without tags — point 1"
  },
  "helpImportS3P2": "The app gives it the name \"Untitled Song\" and key C.",
  "@helpImportS3P2": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Text files without tags — point 2"
  },
  "helpImportS3P3": "You can open and edit its title, chords, key, and tempo at any time.",
  "@helpImportS3P3": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Text files without tags — point 3"
  },
  "helpImportS4Heading": "Duplicate songs",
  "@helpImportS4Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Import › section heading"
  },
  "helpImportS4P1": "If a song has the same title as one in your library, the app follows your duplicate setting.",
  "@helpImportS4P1": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Duplicate songs — point 1"
  },
  "helpImportS4P2": "You can choose to overwrite the existing song, rename the new one, rename the old one, or ask for a title each time.",
  "@helpImportS4P2": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Duplicate songs — point 2"
  },
  "helpImportS4P3": "Set this in Settings → General → Import Settings.",
  "@helpImportS4P3": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Duplicate songs — point 3"
  },
  "helpImportS5Heading": "Check before it is saved",
  "@helpImportS5Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Import › section heading"
  },
  "helpImportS5P1": "Every import stops at a preview screen first.",
  "@helpImportS5P1": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Check before it is saved — point 1"
  },
  "helpImportS5P2": "You can read the titles, artists, keys and words that were found, and fix a title before anything is written.",
  "@helpImportS5P2": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Check before it is saved — point 2"
  },
  "helpImportS5P3": "Nothing reaches your library until you confirm.",
  "@helpImportS5P3": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Check before it is saved — point 3"
  },
  "helpImportS6Heading": "Other ways songs come in",
  "@helpImportS6Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Import › section heading"
  },
  "helpImportS6P1": "Opening a ChordPro file from a file manager, an email or a chat app hands it to LyricChord and opens the same preview.",
  "@helpImportS6P1": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Other ways songs come in — point 1"
  },
  "helpImportS6P2": "A bandmate standing next to you can send songs with no file at all — see the AirQR topic.",
  "@helpImportS6P2": {
    "description": "Help › Import › Other ways songs come in — point 2"
  },
  "titleHelpExport": "Export",
  "@titleHelpExport": {
    "description": "Help › topic title (export)"
  },
  "helpExportSummary": "Save your songs out of the app",
  "@helpExportSummary": {
    "description": "Help › Export › one-line summary on the hub card"
  },
  "helpExportIntro": "Export saves songs as a file you choose the place for. Share hands the same file straight to another app. Everything stays offline — nothing is uploaded, and the system file picker or share sheet does the work.",
  "@helpExportIntro": {
    "description": "Help › Export › opening paragraph"
  },
  "helpExportS1Heading": "Export all songs",
  "@helpExportS1Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Export › section heading"
  },
  "helpExportS1P1": "Go to Settings > General > Import.",
  "@helpExportS1P1": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Export all songs — point 1"
  },
  "helpExportS1P2": "Tap \"Export all songs\".",
  "@helpExportS1P2": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Export all songs — point 2"
  },
  "helpExportS1P3": "Your whole songbook is saved as one ChordPro file.",
  "@helpExportS1P3": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Export all songs — point 3"
  },
  "helpExportS2Heading": "Export some songs (ChordPro)",
  "@helpExportS2Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Export › section heading"
  },
  "helpExportS2P1": "On the Songs list, long-press to select the songs you want.",
  "@helpExportS2P1": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Export some songs (ChordPro) — point 1"
  },
  "helpExportS2P2": "Tap the export icon in the top bar.",
  "@helpExportS2P2": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Export some songs (ChordPro) — point 2"
  },
  "helpExportS2P3": "The selected songs are saved as one ChordPro file.",
  "@helpExportS2P3": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Export some songs (ChordPro) — point 3"
  },
  "helpExportS3Heading": "Export one song",
  "@helpExportS3Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Export › section heading"
  },
  "helpExportS3P1": "Open the song, then the top-bar menu (More options) → \"Export\".",
  "@helpExportS3P1": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Export one song — point 1"
  },
  "helpExportS3P2": "Choose ChordPro (.chordpro) or PDF (.pdf), then tap Export.",
  "@helpExportS3P2": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Export one song — point 2"
  },
  "helpExportS3P3": "The system file saver opens so you can pick where it goes.",
  "@helpExportS3P3": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Export one song — point 3"
  },
  "helpExportS3P4": "Whatever you export uses the key you are looking at, so a song you have transposed is saved in that key.",
  "@helpExportS3P4": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Export one song — point 4"
  },
  "helpExportS4Heading": "What a PDF looks like",
  "@helpExportS4Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Export › section heading"
  },
  "helpExportS4P1": "Title, artist, key and BPM at the top, guitar chord diagrams under that, then the words with the chords above them.",
  "@helpExportS4P1": {
    "description": "Help › Export › What a PDF looks like — point 1"
  },
  "helpExportS4P2": "The words use the lyric font you picked in Settings → Fonts, so Malayalam is shaped correctly and the text stays selectable.",
  "@helpExportS4P2": {
    "description": "Help › Export › What a PDF looks like — point 2"
  },
  "helpExportS4P3": "The page is only as wide as the song needs — a song with short lines gets a narrow, tall page that fills a phone screen better — up to A4 width at the most.",
  "@helpExportS4P3": {
    "description": "Help › Export › What a PDF looks like — point 3"
  },
  "helpExportS4P4": "If a line is still too long, the font is stepped down (never below 9 pt) so it does not wrap in the middle.",
  "@helpExportS4P4": {
    "description": "Help › Export › What a PDF looks like — point 4"
  },
  "helpExportS5Heading": "Share instead of save",
  "@helpExportS5Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Export › section heading"
  },
  "helpExportS5P1": "The top-bar menu also has \"Share\", which opens the system share sheet instead of the file saver.",
  "@helpExportS5P1": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Share instead of save — point 1"
  },
  "helpExportS5P2": "You can share as ChordPro, as PDF, or as an AirQR stream — see the AirQR topic.",
  "@helpExportS5P2": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Share instead of save — point 2"
  },
  "helpExportS5P3": "Selecting several songs on the Songs list gives you the same share choice for the whole set.",
  "@helpExportS5P3": {
    "description": "Help › Export › Share instead of save — point 3"
  },
  "titleHelpAirqr": "AirQR sharing",
  "@titleHelpAirqr": {
    "description": "Help › topic title (airqr)"
  },
  "helpAirqrSummary": "Pass songs to another phone with the camera",
  "@helpAirqrSummary": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › one-line summary on the hub card"
  },
  "helpAirqrIntro": "AirQR moves songs from one phone to another by flashing a run of QR codes on one screen while the other phone watches with its camera. No internet, no Bluetooth, no Wi-Fi, no cable and no account — just two screens facing each other.",
  "@helpAirqrIntro": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › opening paragraph"
  },
  "helpAirqrS1Heading": "Send one song",
  "@helpAirqrS1Heading": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › section heading"
  },
  "helpAirqrS1P1": "Open the song, then the top-bar menu → \"Share\".",
  "@helpAirqrS1P1": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Send one song — point 1"
  },
  "helpAirqrS1P2": "Pick \"AirQR stream\" and tap Share.",
  "@helpAirqrS1P2": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Send one song — point 2"
  },
  "helpAirqrS1P3": "The codes start flashing straight away. Hold the phone still and let the other one read it.",
  "@helpAirqrS1P3": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Send one song — point 3"
  },
  "helpAirqrS1P4": "What goes across is the song as you are looking at it, so a key you have transposed to travels with it.",
  "@helpAirqrS1P4": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Send one song — point 4"
  },
  "helpAirqrS2Heading": "Send several songs",
  "@helpAirqrS2Heading": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › section heading"
  },
  "helpAirqrS2P1": "Settings → General → Import → \"Send all via AirQR\" sends the whole songbook.",
  "@helpAirqrS2P1": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Send several songs — point 1"
  },
  "helpAirqrS2P2": "Or long-press on the Songs list to select some songs and tap the QR icon in the top bar.",
  "@helpAirqrS2P2": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Send several songs — point 2"
  },
  "helpAirqrS3Heading": "Receive",
  "@helpAirqrS3Heading": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › section heading"
  },
  "helpAirqrS3P1": "On the receiving phone, tap the scan icon in the songbook top bar, or go to Settings → General → Import → \"Import via AirQR\".",
  "@helpAirqrS3P1": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Receive — point 1"
  },
  "helpAirqrS3P2": "Point the camera at the sending screen and wait. The panel counts the pieces as they arrive.",
  "@helpAirqrS3P2": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Receive — point 2"
  },
  "helpAirqrS3P3": "When it has everything the phone buzzes and the import preview opens, so you can check the songs before they are saved.",
  "@helpAirqrS3P3": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Receive — point 3"
  },
  "helpAirqrS3P4": "The gallery icon reads a photo of a code instead of the live camera, for a code someone sent you as a picture.",
  "@helpAirqrS3P4": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Receive — point 4"
  },
  "helpAirqrS4Heading": "Getting a clean read",
  "@helpAirqrS4Heading": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › section heading"
  },
  "helpAirqrS4P1": "The song is cut into small pieces shown one after another, with spare repair pieces mixed in, so a frame the camera misses is filled in instead of starting again.",
  "@helpAirqrS4P1": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Getting a clean read — point 1"
  },
  "helpAirqrS4P2": "The \"Stream Speed\" slider on the sending phone runs from 5 to 25 frames a second and starts at 10.",
  "@helpAirqrS4P2": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Getting a clean read — point 2"
  },
  "helpAirqrS4P3": "An older phone or a dim screen reads better slower. Turn the speed down if the count stops moving.",
  "@helpAirqrS4P3": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Getting a clean read — point 3"
  },
  "helpAirqrS4P4": "Keep both screens still and bright, roughly a hand-span apart.",
  "@helpAirqrS4P4": {
    "description": "Help › AirQR sharing › Getting a clean read — point 4"
  },
  "titleHelpAppearance": "Themes & fonts",
  "@titleHelpAppearance": {
    "description": "Help › topic title (appearance)"
  },
  "helpAppearanceSummary": "Make the sheet easy to read",
  "@helpAppearanceSummary": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › one-line summary on the hub card"
  },
  "helpAppearanceIntro": "A sheet read on a dark stage and a sheet read at a desk are not the same job. Three settings cover it: the theme, the lyric font, and how big the text is.",
  "@helpAppearanceIntro": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › opening paragraph"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS1Heading": "Theme",
  "@helpAppearanceS1Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › section heading"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS1P1": "Settings → Themes offers System theme, Light theme and Dark theme.",
  "@helpAppearanceS1P1": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Theme — point 1"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS1P2": "System follows whatever the phone is set to.",
  "@helpAppearanceS1P2": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Theme — point 2"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS1P3": "Dark is easier on the eyes on a stage and easier on the battery.",
  "@helpAppearanceS1P3": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Theme — point 3"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS1P4": "The choice is saved and takes effect at once.",
  "@helpAppearanceS1P4": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Theme — point 4"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS2Heading": "Lyric font",
  "@helpAppearanceS2Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › section heading"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS2P1": "Settings → Fonts picks the font the words are drawn in: System default, Noto Sans Malayalam, Noto Serif Malayalam, Manjari or Gayathri.",
  "@helpAppearanceS2P1": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Lyric font — point 1"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS2P2": "Each choice shows a live sample in English and in Malayalam, so you can see the letter shapes before you pick.",
  "@helpAppearanceS2P2": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Lyric font — point 2"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS2P3": "The Malayalam fonts shape chillu, conjuncts and vowel signs properly. The system font often does not.",
  "@helpAppearanceS2P3": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Lyric font — point 3"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS2P4": "One choice covers the whole app, and the exported PDF uses the same font.",
  "@helpAppearanceS2P4": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Lyric font — point 4"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS2P5": "The fonts are bundled with the app under an open licence and are listed on the licences page in About.",
  "@helpAppearanceS2P5": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Lyric font — point 5"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS3Heading": "Text size",
  "@helpAppearanceS3Heading": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › section heading"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS3P1": "Pinch the words with two fingers to make the text bigger or smaller, from 10 up to 32.",
  "@helpAppearanceS3P1": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Text size — point 1"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS3P2": "It works on the ordinary song screen and in full screen, and it does not disturb the scrolling.",
  "@helpAppearanceS3P2": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Text size — point 2"
  },
  "helpAppearanceS3P3": "The pitch sheet also has five fixed sizes — 85%, 95%, 100%, 115% and 130% — which multiply whatever the pinch has set. Use those to set a stage size once and keep it.",
  "@helpAppearanceS3P3": {
    "description": "Help › Themes & fonts › Text size — point 3"
  },
